# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
#
# .gitignore is LAST-MATCH-WINS, so ordering matters: the broad catch-all comes
# first, then the specific files that must be tracked, then a final re-ignore of
# anything that must never be committed regardless of what came before.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Catch-all: assume any JSON is a service account or config dump until proven otherwise.
*.json

# Project files that must be tracked (checked in and safe - no credentials).
!version.json
!google-services.template.json

# Environment and credential files, in any directory.
.env
.env.*
**/secrets.properties
**/secrets.xml
**/api_keys.xml
**/service-account*.json
**/credentials*.json
*.p12
*.pfx
*.der

# Final word: these must never be committed, whatever any rule above says.
# Listed last so no negation can re-expose them.
**/google-services.json
**/google-services*.json
.firebase/
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/keystore.properties
**/local.properties

# Others
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*~

KNOWN_ISSUES.md
